CVSign 2/3: CCA and CVA modules (Eqs. 1-10) in place of CorrNet's correlation

Why: no CVSign code is published (preference level 3 for these modules only).
CVSign's visual encoder is CorrNet's 2D-as-3D ResNet (1x3x3 / 1x1x1 kernels,
modules inserted after layers 2, 3 and 4 with zero-initialised residual gates)
with Get_Correlation replaced by the paper's CCA + CVA and a ResNet34 backbone
"pretrained on ImageNet" (Implementation Details). Upstream resnet34() builds
the network without loading weights, so it now loads them exactly as
resnet18() does. CCA's affinity is recomputed in backward (torch checkpoint)
instead of stored; it contains no normalisation or randomness, so gradients
are unchanged. Unstated values (C_hid, heads, Conv_Block norm/activation,
boundary handling) are marked as guesses inline and in the README.
Applies to: CorrNet @ 5a361cc709ae8f697f4c9e23760e64c2daa8f744
